      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Compute $P(X\\ge 2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2-2x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(2\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{2-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{2-2x}]}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
